  "notes": [
    "orbit_asof comes from gp_history: the orbit as of each epoch, taken only from element sets already on file at or before obs_date, so it never leaks the future. orbit_terminal is satcat's one terminal snapshot -- leaky for decayed objects -- kept only for the *_leaky_orbit ablation comparison.",
    "perigee_decay_rate_km_per_day is negative while an object is losing altitude. element_age_days says how stale the matched element set was; rows past MAX_ELEMENT_AGE_DAYS have orbit_asof nulled out rather than guessed.",
    "space_weather_forward requires a solar forecast at inference time.",
    "Drop event_observed == 0 rows for plain regression; keep them for survival models."
